From: Prabhsimran Singh <prabhsimrans@nvidia.com>
Subject: llama: draw the temperature-sampled rows of a batched step together

Batched serving gave every row of a sequence with a [temp, dist] sampler
chain its own sampler graph: a scale, softmax, cumulative sum and threshold
over the whole vocabulary per row. The rows of all such sequences are now
gathered once and drawn together, each scaled by its own inverse temperature
and compared with its own uniform draw, which the dist sampler fills from its
generator in the same order as before.

Attaching or detaching a sampler no longer re-reserves the scheduler in
batched serving (worst-case prefill and decode graphs on the next decode):
the sampling subgraph is built every step and its compute buffer grows on
demand.

Upstream: not planned (batched serving path).

